    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GtzUm5hXcLmjePs7nN39W2)_\n\nSia's rule: the `.org` doc is authoritative for what is committed. `sp-search-browsing-trails.org` no longer has `counsel-recoll-function` and `counsel-recoll` (removed in 8b08da2), so `sp-search.el` is re-tangled without them: 27 lines removed, nothing else changes.\n\n- The `R` menu entry stays: it is guarded by `(fboundp 'counsel-recoll)`, so it is simply hidden now.\n- Only `sp-search.el` is touched. The `sp-org-insert-inline-comment` rename (doc binding and `.el`) and the tag-groups drift are in #252, which this does not overlap, **except** that #252 also puts the Recoll definitions back into the doc. That part of #252 contradicts Sia's instruction and should be dropped there, or this PR is undone.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container); the removed block is exactly the one the doc lost.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCP1EeS4LxrGn5uw6X)_",
